To display a matrix as a bitmap with a zoom feature in Qt, you can follow these steps:

1. Create a QMatrix object to represent your matrix.
2. Create a QPixmap object to store the bitmap representation of your matrix.
3. Implement a zoom function that adjusts the size of the QPixmap and the QMatrix accordingly.
4. Display the QPixmap in a QLabel or other Qt widget.

Here's some sample code to get you started:
```cpp
#include <QApplication>
#include <QMatrix>
#include <QPixmap>
#include <QLabel>

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    QApplication app(argc, argv);

    // Create a QMatrix object to represent your matrix
    QMatrix matrix;
    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < 4; j++) {
            matrix.set(i, j, i * j);
        }
    }

    // Create a QPixmap object to store the bitmap representation of your matrix
    QPixmap pixmap(matrix.size(), QImage::Format_RGB32);

    // Implement a zoom function that adjusts the size of the QPixmap and the QMatrix accordingly
    void zoom(qreal factor) {
        matrix.scale(factor, factor);
        pixmap.resize(matrix.size());
    }

    // Display the QPixmap in a QLabel or other Qt widget
